{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars","id":759142,"title":"[3E] Are there still 300 Solars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T12:28:08-08:00","id":759142,"title":"[3E] Are there still 300 Solars?","content":"I can't find any reference anywhere in the book to Solars being enumerated at 300. Or Lunars, for that matter. Sidereals are specified to be only 100, but it's in an odd place in a throwaway line under the Exigents entry - it's mentioned nowhere else.<br /> <br /> Is this another thing left deliberately vague in 3rd edition, how many Celestial Exalts there actually are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2196-riklurt","name":"Riklurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:31:26-08:00","id":759175,"title":"","content":"I think it's deliberately left vague, but part of me WANTS to say that in some post somewhere, it's ballparked at &quot;Around&quot; 300 Solars and around 400 Lunars. 100 Sids exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:32:35-08:00","id":759178,"title":"","content":"As far as i recall everything is being kept vague because hard numbers suck the fun and mystery out of myth telling. Abyssals and infernals may not be entirely taken from solars. Alchemicals were bumming around in the first age. all is vaguer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:33:23-08:00","id":759180,"title":"","content":"Is is 300 Solars, or 300 Solars, Infernals, and Abyssals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:38:41-08:00","id":759186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759180#post759180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is is 300 Solars, or 300 Solars, Infernals, and Abyssals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. See, THIS is why I like using the term Solaroid, despite it apparently having people who hate it with as much anger and vitriol as I've seen directed at the term 'Magitech'. I mean, between &quot;Solaroid&quot;, &quot;Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals&quot;, or &quot;Solars and their dark reflections&quot;, one's just flat-out easier to say.<br /> <br /> I think in Second Edition it was ~300 Solaroids, with 50 being Infernals and ~100 being Abyssals. Which, also, yeah, they used the word &quot;Around&quot; quite liberally when counting the numbers in 2E. Nowhere did it say &quot;There are exactly 300 Solars&quot; that I saw in the core, nor did it say that they managed to capture exactly 150 Exaltations to make into Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> It's just that people round to a nice convenient number. I know that I, personally, would get a bit twitchy if it turned out there were 297 Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:43:22-08:00","id":759194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759186#post759186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno. See, THIS is why I like using the term Solaroid, despite it apparently having people who hate it with as much anger and vitriol as I've seen directed at the term 'Magitech'. I mean, between &quot;Solaroid&quot;, &quot;Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals&quot;, or &quot;Solars and their dark reflections&quot;, one's just flat-out easier to say.<br /> <br /> I think in Second Edition it was ~300 Solaroids, with 50 being Infernals and ~100 being Abyssals. Which, also, yeah, they used the word &quot;Around&quot; quite liberally when counting the numbers in 2E. Nowhere did it say &quot;There are exactly 300 Solars&quot; that I saw in the core, nor did it say that they managed to capture exactly 150 Exaltations to make into Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> It's just that people round to a nice convenient number. I know that I, personally, would get a bit twitchy if it turned out there were 297 Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;AUGGHH, JUST EXALT 3 MORE SOLARS! I DON'T CARE, I NEED THAT NUMBER TO MATCH!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:44:05-08:00","id":759195,"title":"","content":"I will happily stop using the term Solaroid when someone comes up with another word that encompassed all humans whose power is derived from the might of a Solar exaltation.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:44:11-08:00","id":759196,"title":"","content":"Given developer comments, it's probably approximately 300 Solars (total, including altered ones), 400 Lunars, precisely 100 Sidereals. It might be mentioned in a later book, but I think it not being mentioned here has less to do with mystery and more with being a low priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:44:41-08:00","id":759197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759194#post759194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;AUGGHH, JUST EXALT 3 MORE SOLARS! I DON'T CARE, I NEED THAT NUMBER TO MATCH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And then Luna would Exalt Lunar #301, because she's a bitch sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:50:55-08:00","id":759204,"title":"","content":"The number of Solars wasn't fixed until some throwaway line about there being 60 Twilights in Book of Three Circles got taken as the Gospel Truth.<br /> <br /> Would be nice to get back to letting Storytellers set such things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Planned Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"http://worldunbent.com\" target=\"_blank\">Legends of a World Unbent</a> - also hosts my Minecraft servers. : )","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2860-vekseid","name":"Vekseid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2860_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:29:04-08:00","id":759270,"title":"","content":"Wait, 400 Lunars? Where'd the extra 100 come from? Did I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2196-riklurt","name":"Riklurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:35:51-08:00","id":759283,"title":"","content":"I always thought the 300 thing was a reference to Spartans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:42:06-08:00","id":759287,"title":"","content":"Well one of the Devs said a while back when talking about Lunars, that the Lunar Mate &quot;thing&quot; kind of went away because their were more Lunars then Solars (and Lunar players hated it). They then said their was something like 350-450 Lunars (they left the number very vague) to the 300 Solars. So unless they've changed their minds since then (which is entirely possible) then there should only be 300 Solar-ish Exalts. That post was a few months ago, so they might have changed their minds.<br /> <br /> It's also likely that the statement that clarified how many their are, was cut. We know for a fact that a lot was cut at the last minute due to word count restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 11-06-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:17:55-08:00","id":759343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riklurt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759270#post759270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, 400 Lunars? Where'd the extra 100 come from? Did I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd edition cut the number down from 1st in order to make it match the Solars. Without the 1:1 bond, it doesn't need to be the case, so one hundred more Lunars! Or perhaps just ninety-nine, floating through the autumn breeze...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:27:51-08:00","id":759347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riklurt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759270#post759270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, 400 Lunars? Where'd the extra 100 come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were always there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:30:22-08:00","id":759349,"title":"","content":"You just didn't notice because <i>eh</i>, when's the last time a Lunar did something notable anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:35:15-08:00","id":759355,"title":"","content":"There are no mortals in Creation. All of them are Lunars, some of whom inexplicably keep turning into Dragon-blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:42:13-08:00","id":759366,"title":"","content":"Wait. Waaaaait. Logic suggests...<br /> <br /> Everyone is a Lunar.<br /> Everyone is the Green Lady.<br /> Therefore, the Green Lady is a Lunar?<br /> <br /> That doesn't add up. I think your premise is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:43:24-08:00","id":759369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759366#post759366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. Waaaaait. Logic suggests...<br /> <br /> Everyone is a Lunar.<br /> Everyone is the Green Lady.<br /> Therefore, the Green Lady is a Lunar?<br /> <br /> That doesn't add up. I think your premise is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>or that the Lunars are the Green Lady?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:44:34-08:00","id":759372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759366#post759366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. Waaaaait. Logic suggests...<br /> <br /> Everyone is a Lunar.<br /> Everyone is the Green Lady.<br /> Therefore, the Green Lady is a Lunar?<br /> <br /> That doesn't add up. I think your premise is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget, all Green Lady Lunars are also the Mirror Flag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:45:46-08:00","id":759373,"title":"","content":"But, wait, isn't everyone in Exalted just Luna wearing a different hat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:08:46-08:00","id":759407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759287#post759287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well one of the Devs said a while back when talking about Lunars, that the Lunar Mate &quot;thing&quot; kind of went away because their were more Lunars then Solars (and Lunar players hated it). They then said their was something like 350-450 Lunars (they left the number very vague) to the 300 Solars. So unless they've changed their minds since then (which is entirely possible) then there should only be 300 Solar-ish Exalts. That post was a few months ago, so they might have changed their minds.<br /> <br /> It's also likely that the statement that clarified how many their are, was cut. We know for a fact that a lot was cut at the last minute due to word count restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players hated the Solar bond, but for some reasons we still got way too many solar bond charms. I've never even heard of anyone who bought those.<br /> 1e edition's Eternal Vow was awesome, though. I hope it (or something like it) comes back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 11-06-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:12:07-08:00","id":759466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759407#post759407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Players hated the Solar bond</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh screw you, don't go putting words in my mouth. I <b>loved</b> the Solar-Lunar Bond. Was it implemented well? Probably not. But the <b>idea</b> of this bond echoing across time, lives, and ages, manifesting in countless ways, is something I adore, and I'm <b>glad</b> that we've still got it.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know how &quot;ONE Integrity charm that provides a way for the Lunar to get around their Solar's stubbornness&quot; counts as &quot;Way too many solar bond charms&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:39:42-08:00","id":759496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759466#post759466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh screw you, don't go putting words in my mouth. I <b>loved</b> the Solar-Lunar Bond. Was it implemented well? Probably not. But the <b>idea</b> of this bond echoing across time, lives, and ages, manifesting in countless ways, is something I adore, and I'm <b>glad</b> that we've still got it.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know how &quot;ONE Integrity charm that provides a way for the Lunar to get around their Solar's stubbornness&quot; counts as &quot;Way too many solar bond charms&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, overreacting much? I was replying to TalosX's comment notably that part:<b> the Lunar Mate &quot;thing&quot; kind of went away because their were more Lunars then Solars (and <u>Lunar players hated it</u>)</b>. It had <b>nothing</b> to do with you.<br /> Solar Bond was a 2e edition Lunar merit on which several Charms were based. That's what I talking about. Not the idea of Solar/Lunar pairings. I even mentioned Eternal Vow to as an earlier implementation of the concept I prefered to the 2e merit.<br /> Do try to actually read what people write before insulting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:43:53-08:00","id":759497,"title":"","content":"I had Solar Bond 5, but the ST had me change it to Eternal Vow (from 1st ed), so I didn't buy any of the Solar Bond charms because they didn't work. I'm not sure if I would anyway: not because I hate them, but because they aren't particularly interesting charms (get some extra dice or successes on occasional rolls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:19:18-08:00","id":759556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759496#post759496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, overreacting much? I was replying to TalosX's comment notably that part:<b> the Lunar Mate &quot;thing&quot; kind of went away because their were more Lunars then Solars (and <u>Lunar players hated it</u>)</b>. It had <b>nothing</b> to do with you.<br /> Solar Bond was a 2e edition Lunar merit on which several Charms were based. That's what I talking about. Not the idea of Solar/Lunar pairings. I even mentioned Eternal Vow to as an earlier implementation of the concept I prefered to the 2e merit.<br /> Do try to actually read what people write before insulting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even worse than a merit; it was a Background, so the very, very marginal fourth and fifth dots that were almost guaranteed to totally sink your Mental DVs were double cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:30:31-08:00","id":759566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759556#post759556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even worse than a merit; it was a Background, so the very, very marginal fourth and fifth dots that were almost guaranteed to totally sink your Mental DVs were double cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That in itself was kind of harsh, given that the one benefitting from it was the Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:50:31-08:00","id":759575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759496#post759496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, overreacting much? I was replying to TalosX's comment notably that part:<b> the Lunar Mate &quot;thing&quot; kind of went away because their were more Lunars then Solars (and <u>Lunar players hated it</u>)</b>. It had <b>nothing</b> to do with you.<br /> Solar Bond was a 2e edition Lunar merit on which several Charms were based. That's what I talking about. Not the idea of Solar/Lunar pairings. I even mentioned Eternal Vow to as an earlier implementation of the concept I prefered to the 2e merit.<br /> Do try to actually read what people write before insulting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, for some reason I assumed we were still on Ex3, and the comment of &quot;Players hated the Solar Bond&quot; sounded like one of those generalizing sweeps, like &quot;Magitech is bad for the system&quot; or the like. I apologize for my outburst, I'm just used to seeing people dismiss things about the game I really like. Yeah, you're right, I should have read more closely.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, I won't argue that the Solar Bond BACKGROUND was a bag of dicks)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:54:41-08:00","id":759580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759575#post759575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, for some reason I assumed we were still on Ex3, and the comment of &quot;Players hated the Solar Bond&quot; sounded like one of those generalizing sweeps, like &quot;Magitech is bad for the system&quot; or the like. I apologize for my outburst, I'm just used to seeing people dismiss things about the game I really like. Yeah, you're right, I should have read more closely.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, I won't argue that the Solar Bond BACKGROUND was a bag of dicks)</div> </div> </div> </div>S'okay, no hard feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:53:33-08:00","id":759626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759575#post759575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, for some reason I assumed we were still on Ex3, and the comment of &quot;Players hated the Solar Bond&quot; sounded like one of those generalizing sweeps, like &quot;Magitech is bad for the system&quot; or the like. I apologize for my outburst, I'm just used to seeing people dismiss things about the game I really like. Yeah, you're right, I should have read more closely.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, I won't argue that the Solar Bond BACKGROUND was a bag of dicks)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Anteros was more commenting on the implementation of the Solar/Lunar Bond in the 2e system. Idea's and implementation can work at cross purposes. Just as I can say that 2e Magitech <b>was</b> bad for the system. Not that it was a bad idea, just that the implementation (fighter-jets, supercomputer AI, and aircraft carriers) became toxic to the setting.<br /> <br /> The Solar/Lunar Bond is still present, but is completely optional for each player. Also they're just Intimacies at the moment. Until we get some actual clarification (likely not until the Lunar book), it's difficult to say what any actual mechanical benefits will exist, if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:58:34-08:00","id":759627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759626#post759626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Anteros was more commenting on the implementation of the Solar/Lunar Bond in the 2e system. Idea's and implementation can work at cross purposes. Just as I can say that 2e Magitech <b>was</b> bad for the system. Not that it was a bad idea, just that the implementation (fighter-jets, supercomputer AI, and aircraft carriers) became toxic to the setting.<br /> <br /> The Solar/Lunar Bond is still present, but is completely optional for each player. Also they're just Intimacies at the moment. Until we get some actual clarification (likely not until the Lunar book), it's difficult to say what any actual mechanical benefits will exist, if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I've realized my mistake, and I admit I was <i>way</i> out of line.<br /> <br /> (Also I'll politely keep my Animating Intelligence Spirits and my Power Armor magitech in my games, thanks)<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm curious to see how the Bond will manifest in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:03:10-08:00","id":759633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759627#post759627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, I'm curious to see how the Bond will manifest in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to EX3, it mostly seems to manifest in the Lunars changing in the wake of the Solars' mass deaths during the Usurpation. Basically, it's a big part of the reasons that their castes aren't the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:10:22-08:00","id":759636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759633#post759633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to EX3, it mostly seems to manifest in the Lunars changing in the wake of the Solars' mass deaths during the Usurpation. Basically, it's a big part of the reasons that their castes aren't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember someone on the forums asking &quot;So, is the Bond gone? Since it says the Bond was broken...&quot; and one of the writers, I think Vance or Holden, said &quot;... Yeah, it was broken <i>by all the Solars dying</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, I mean like, mechanically. The mechanic of the Lunars being able to get around Stubborn Boar Defense is a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:39:38-08:00","id":759651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759627#post759627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also I'll politely keep my Animating Intelligence Spirits and my Power Armor magitech in my games, thanks)<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm curious to see how the Bond will manifest in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>LoL, nothing wrong with Animating intelligence Spirits or Power Armor. I believe the Devs have said both of those still exist in one form or another. It was some of the crazier stuff that really upset the game balance and theme. I mean if you want to have a crystal ball that stores vast quantities of information, that's great. To have a no-shit computer with monitors, keyboard, etc is just out of theme. It was magitech with almost no &quot;magi&quot; involved. It just got silly!<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to the Lunar book. One of my favorite gaming-buddies (or gal rather) is really excited by the Lunar themes. She's never played Exalted before, so its great to see her so excited. She's planning to role a Night caste until Lunar's releases. In Star Wars, she's played a very interesting Ewok assassin/thief. I'm actually a little concerned with the trouble she'll cause as a Night caste or Lunar! It should be awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:20:16-08:00","id":759667,"title":"","content":"There are five solars. The rest have faded beyond memory, gone ahead to a place and time not known to man. The light is fading, and you are the last.<br /> <br /> There are fifty solars. Never more than an exalted few, it was their inspiration and example more than their raw power that led the way for their brethren. No longer.<br /> <br /> There are three hundred solars. Three hundred bickering god-kings who made the world kneel, and were knelt in turn.<br /> <br /> There are three thousand solars. Three thousand lights who stretched forth the wings of Creation, made its borders greater and stronger than they had ever been before, and were swallowed up by its sheer size.<br /> <br /> Do the exact numbers matter? The real question is, &quot;how many Solars have you met, and how many will you meet?&quot;<br /> (And how many of them want to fight you, and how many of them want to have sex with you?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 11-06-2015, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:50:19-08:00","id":759679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759667#post759667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are five solars. The rest have faded beyond memory, gone ahead to a place and time not known to man. The light is fading, and you are the last.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE this i hope you dont mind if i steal it for a game! The idea of just 5, one circle, thats all left in creation is an awesome story idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:55:58-08:00","id":759686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759679#post759679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I LOVE this i hope you dont mind if i steal it for a game! The idea of just 5, one circle, thats all left in creation is an awesome story idea!</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do! Nothing would make me happier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:27:24-08:00","id":759705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759186#post759186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in Second Edition it was ~300 Solaroids, with 50 being Infernals and ~100 being Abyssals. Which, also, yeah, they used the word &quot;Around&quot; quite liberally when counting the numbers in 2E. Nowhere did it say &quot;There are exactly 300 Solars&quot; that I saw in the core, nor did it say that they managed to capture exactly 150 Exaltations to make into Abyssals and Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I feel like MoEP: Abyssals lays out that after the Jade Prison was broke 150 Solar Exaltations were recovered, with the Yozi claiming exactly 50 and the Neverborn claimed 100 (although they had expected more). <br /> <br /> The thing that always got me was that, since you could turn a Solar into an Abyssal much more easily than the reverse, and since &quot;Former Circlemate is now a dread Abyssal enemy&quot; was a thing in the Quick adventures, scroll of Exalts, etc. the numbers actually always seemed ready to make pure Solar Exaltations the second largest Solaroid faction. I don't remember if the details were ever broken down (or if it was just a table joke), but weren't there close to 123 canon Abyssals versus 127 Solars by the end of 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:38:49-08:00","id":759717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759667#post759667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And how many of them want to fight you, and how many of them want to have sex with you?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers typically are equal, and there is a surprising amount of overlap.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the numbers being vague as an OOC concept. Now, I'm ALL FOR the <i>characters</i> believing there are limited numbers, and exactly how many of each type exist, but there is always room for a difference between character knowledge and reality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:39:18-08:00","id":759718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759705#post759705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I feel like MoEP: Abyssals lays out that after the Jade Prison was broke 150 Solar Exaltations were recovered, with the Yozi claiming exactly 50 and the Neverborn claimed 100 (although they had expected more).</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember it being mentioned that the Yozi had showed the Neverborn how to corrupt Exaltations, and in exchange said &quot;When you claim them from their prison, we want fifty. Exactly.&quot; They expected the Neverborn would grab like, seventy or so, but they did MUCH better than anticipated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:55:23-08:00","id":759848,"title":"","content":"The Bond is still a Thing; it's just not a thing that attaches to every Lunar. Some Lunars seem to trade off their Bond for a rage that drives them to tear down the Realm and fight the Sidereals. Other Lunars had no Bond, probably because was a tricksy bitch (in a good way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:15:37-08:00","id":759852,"title":"","content":"As such a controversial thing, with players who both hated and liked the Bond, saying that some have it and some don't (so, you can choose whether your Lunar does or doesn't have it) seems the best policy, and that's what the devs (sensibly) seem to be doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:28:56-08:00","id":759860,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of some sort of bond, but not something thats part of the Exaltation itself. I like the idea that strong feelings developed in a previous life carry over. That creates something similar in some pairs(or tios, or quartets, or...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), but not all Lunars will be like that. And that way it can also go the other way, with the Solar feeling a bond as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:39:16-08:00","id":759866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Lunars seem to trade off their Bond for a rage that drives them to tear down the Realm and fight the Sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't read that as a trade off so much as an insatiable itch that develops when the subject of the Bond is no longer around. Although that doesn't seem to be focused solely on the Solars, the ruins of the Realm also look like a driving force for it. Perhaps that might be similar to my prior idea that what the First Age Lunars needed wasn't quite the Solars so much as a sense of connection and dedication to <i>something</i>, and while the Solars were a very powerful and prestigious subject for that attachment, that role of guardians of the Realm could also emerge from it. That might be part of why some of them can direct their fury at more personal goals, even if many are trying to be free from it altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:52:13-08:00","id":759871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759651#post759651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LoL, nothing wrong with Animating intelligence Spirits or Power Armor. I believe the Devs have said both of those still exist in one form or another. It was some of the crazier stuff that really upset the game balance and theme. I mean if you want to have a crystal ball that stores vast quantities of information, that's great. To have a no-shit computer with monitors, keyboard, etc is just out of theme. It was magitech with almost no &quot;magi&quot; involved. It just got silly!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, 3ed seems to generally imply that many higher artefacts have <i>some</i> level of sentience, although not in the sense of &quot;concious or self-aware&quot;, and more on the level of &quot;If Spring Razor doesn't like you, its evocations won't work for you&quot;. But we also do have one concious, self-aware sentient artefact in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:53:08-08:00","id":759872,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Everyone Hated the Bond&quot; mostly refers to the 2e implementation, which despite vocal objections to it, Glories then expanded with the Solar charms to forcibly upgrade your mate to Solar Bond 5 and perfectly locate the bonded Lunar, and to make remote social attacks against the bonded Lunar. It was really creepy.<br /> <br /> I do like the concept of bonded across eternity. I just am more optimistic about 3e's setup since it feels both OOCly voluntary [sure, my recently exalted Lunar character didn't agree to it because it was who she was in the first age rather than now, but I as a player don't have to buy into it if I don't feel like it] and more give-and-take rather than &quot;Mechanically this is basically magically enforced one-way subservience.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:08:16-08:00","id":759881,"title":"","content":"I would also say that, given a lot of comments about Solars encountering Lunars and finding them to be quite different to any of their memories of companions to a past life, closing that gap may entail quite a bit more effort on the part of the actors, even if the Lunar in question is not hostile to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:27:12-08:00","id":759913,"title":"","content":"What seems clear is that there is a bond, that it's nature has changed, and that it is affecting the Lunars' exaltations rather than the Solars', like in 2e.<br /> I wonder if a Solar could now find herself with 2 Lunar mates? Or if a Lunar could have a bond to someone other than a Solar?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T06:52:46-08:00","id":759964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759466#post759466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh screw you, don't go putting words in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you and Anteros have cleared up this misunderstanding but please don't talk to other posters like this in future.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:34:03-08:00","id":760000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759633#post759633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to EX3, it mostly seems to manifest in the Lunars changing in the wake of the Solars' mass deaths during the Usurpation. Basically, it's a big part of the reasons that their castes aren't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We broke the Castes ourselves, to better adapt to this brave new world we found ourselves in, where retainers were hailed as conquering hero-kings, with the rightful lords reviled as the most terrible of demons&quot; &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &quot;wahhhhhhh we hit in the wyld doing nothing and it was mean and broke us wahhhhhhhhhhhhhh&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:46:27-08:00","id":760005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=759196#post759196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given developer comments, it's probably approximately 300 Solars (total, including altered ones), 400 Lunars, precisely 100 Sidereals. It might be mentioned in a later book, but I think it not being mentioned here has less to do with mystery and more with being a low priority.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it was pointed out somewhere that the one developer comment we had on the subject was more or less a direct quote from the 1st edition Storyteller's Guide. I'm also pretty sure that I haven't seen anything that suggests that 300 Solars is meant to include Abyssals and Infernals. I haven't seen anything to suggest that it doesn't either, but considering the devs have made it clear that they're going to give less hard facts, and that there's going to be some major changes with how both Abyssals and Infernals, I feel like being open to the possiblity that things might be different is the best course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:07:37-08:00","id":760054,"title":"","content":"The original STC said about 150 Solars, about 100 Abyssals, about 400 Lunars, 100 Sidereals and around 10,000 DBs in the Realm. Note that the Solar + Abyssal numbers there is around 250, which if the &quot;50 Infenrals&quot; thing hangs about, does total 300ish Solar Exaltations.<br /> <br /> That being said, we're more likely to hear if it ever comes up in the books that htere's 150ish Solars now and not really much dwelling on how many there were back in the day.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:10:19-08:00","id":760056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=760054#post760054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, we're more likely to hear if it ever comes up in the books that htere's 150ish Solars now and not really much dwelling on how many there were back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but given it really doesn't matter at all, we might not get even this. Which is fine imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:42:26-08:00","id":760073,"title":"","content":"I think that dev comments have indicated that 50 specific Exaltations were requested by the Yozis, whatever that means in the context. It was questioned whether they were the worst of the First Age Solars, or the best, as well, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:53:43-08:00","id":760123,"title":"","content":"My preferred numbers are 275 Solars (about 20ish of which were not bound), 100 Abyssals, 50 Infernals, and 425 Lunars.<br /> <br /> Thus there were originally one Solar and one Lunar for every day/night of the year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T12:52:44-08:00","id":760149,"title":"","content":"I guess the point I was sort of obliquely trying to make was that the difference between 275 solars and 300 solars and 325 solars is immaterial so go with whatever you like. (I really like one for every day of the year, though.)<br /> <br /> The point at which it actually makes a difference lies on orders of magnitude. At 5, the PCs are It. At 50, they're ridiculously rare and each one has to acquire and leverage massive resources instead of relying on their own (albeit considerable) power to change things and a circle is still this region-shattering confluence of incredible powers. At 500, there's room for circles aplenty and running into Solars throughout Creation but each one is a singular event. At 5000 they'll make a huge and devastating splash world-wide and running into them in big cities or important events isn't even weird (this is the place I honestly think most sandbox games with turnover are at; Celestial Exalts come and go and nobody's wondering if there's a Creation-wide depletion of them to fill Nexus). At 50,000 you live in a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WorldOfHam\" target=\"_blank\">World of Ham</a>.<br /> <br /> A few hundred is probably ideal though. A few dozen involves Solars in a world that may well not need them any more. A few thousand involves Solars in a world that probably doesn't <i>want</i> them. (Just a few involves Solars in a world that <i>desperately</i> needs them and doesn't have any.) Those are all completely valid play modes, but a good &quot;default&quot; is in the middle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:22:19-08:00","id":760319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=760149#post760149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I really like one for every day of the year, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I, also, really like the 1 per the day of the year. Great idea, glamourweaver. Though doesn't Calibration not have a moon? I think I'd rather 420 Lunars in light of that. I also like the 'first circle' oblique implied by Epiphany's novels, a circle that had one of each Caste that were exemplary in their (2e) Caste abilities but had no ability to learn outside that (and I think no Lunar bonds). <br /> <br /> Regarding 5 or a dozen Solars, that sounds like a great premise to bake into a Shogunate setting.<br /> <br /> Regarding thousands of Solars, I think I'd like to play that best in a Gunstar Autocthonia setting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:21:27-08:00","id":760356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=760319#post760319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, also, really like the 1 per the day of the year. Great idea, glamourweaver. Though doesn't Calibration not have a moon? I think I'd rather <b>420 Lunars</b> in light of that. I also like the 'first circle' oblique implied by Epiphany's novels, a circle that had one of each Caste that were exemplary in their (2e) Caste abilities but had no ability to learn outside that (and I think no Lunar bonds).<br /> <br /> Regarding 5 or a dozen Solars, that sounds like a great premise to bake into a Shogunate setting.<br /> <br /> Regarding thousands of Solars, I think I'd like to play that best in a Gunstar Autocthonia setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>BLAZE IT SHAPESHIFT EVERY DAY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T19:32:58-08:00","id":760412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=760356#post760356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BLAZE IT SHAPESHIFT EVERY DAY</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, what if we could, like, change who we are man? Like, completely? I heard this Native American story where the coyote god would stalk another god and rip their heart out and eat it just to pull some practical joke with their shape. He was the best trickster in the whole pantheon, man! If he was even, like a dude, though. What if he was a she? Mind. Blown.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:17:27-08:00","id":760473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759142-3e-are-there-still-300-solars?p=760356#post760356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BLAZE IT SHAPESHIFT EVERY DAY</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest to god that's why I went with 425 and not 420.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:25:17-08:00","id":760477,"title":"","content":"Hmm, what if we made it 365 Solars, one for every day. Just leave it as a clue that something about Creation changed after the War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:28:38-08:00","id":760478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sol